    "result_text": "All 28 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field, derived from the owner's city via the fixed city-to-region table, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived read-only fields (like `displayName`, `membershipTier`).\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. This generates the `locality` field (with getter/setter) on the generated `OwnerDto`, so MapStruct auto-maps it by name from the model.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `getLocality()` method backed by a fixed `CITY_REGION` map (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\nMapStruct's `toOwnerDto` auto-maps `getLocality()` \u2192 `setLocality()` by name (same mechanism the other derived fields rely on), so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `locality` in its JSON.\n\nThe full acceptance suite (28 tests, including the new `Cp17Tests`) is green.",
